issue.description:
Add a new built-in Personal UI theme named **Amber Dusk**, using the owner-provided light/dark token set as the source palette.

This should be implemented as a normal built-in Theme v3 preset, not as a parallel CSS/theme system.

## Overall direction

The owner provided a complete shadcn/Tailwind-style token stylesheet containing:

* light-mode semantic colors;
* dark-mode semantic colors;
* chart colors;
* dedicated Sidebar colors;
* typography families;
* radius;
* shadow values;
* tracking;
* spacing.

Use those supplied values as the source of truth for the new built-in theme, then reconcile them into the existing Personal UI Theme v3 model and preset architecture.

Theme name:

**Amber Dusk**

Do not paste the entire source stylesheet into the product as a second styling layer.

Instead:

source token stylesheet
→ reconcile supported values
→ map into existing Theme v3 fields
→ register as built-in theme preset

