## 3. Typography source values

The source stylesheet uses:

```css
--font-sans: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji', 'Segoe UI Symbol', 'Noto Color Emoji';
--font-serif: ui-serif, Georgia, Cambria, "Times New Roman", Times, serif;
--font-mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
--tracking-normal: 0em;
```

Map only the typography fields supported by the current Theme v3 contract.

Do not introduce new font roles merely because the source stylesheet contains them.

## 4. Radius / spacing source values

Source values:

```css
--radius: 0.5rem;
--spacing: 0.25rem;
```

Map these into the accepted Theme v3 geometry/spacing model where equivalent fields already exist.

Do not create new schema fields solely to mirror this source format.

## 5. Shadow source values

Source values:

```css
--shadow-x: 0;
--shadow-y: 1px;
--shadow-blur: 3px;
--shadow-spread: 0px;
--shadow-opacity: 0.1;
--shadow-color: oklch(0 0 0);

--shadow-2xs: 0 1px 3px 0px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.05);
--shadow-xs: 0 1px 3px 0px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.05);
--shadow-sm: 0 1px 3px 0px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10), 0 1px 2px -1px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10);
--shadow: 0 1px 3px 0px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10), 0 1px 2px -1px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10);
--shadow-md: 0 1px 3px 0px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10), 0 2px 4px -1px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10);
--shadow-lg: 0 1px 3px 0px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10), 0 4px 6px -1px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10);
--shadow-xl: 0 1px 3px 0px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10), 0 8px 10px -1px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.10);
--shadow-2xl: 0 1px 3px 0px hsl(0 0% 0% / 0.25);
```

Use the accepted Personal UI shadow model.

If Theme v3 stores only a subset or higher-level shadow values, reconcile the source into that model rather than adding parallel raw shadow variables.

## 6. Built-in theme behavior

Register **Amber Dusk** as a normal built-in theme alongside existing built-in presets.

Requirements:

* appears in the existing theme selector/preset flow;
* switching to Amber Dusk updates the live Workbench immediately;
* light/dark mode uses the supplied paired values;
* dedicated Sidebar values are preserved;
* chart colors are preserved;
* theme reset/default/history behavior remains coherent;
* saving/forking/comparing themes continues to work;
* import/export remains compatible with the existing Theme v3 format;
* Design Command continues to operate on Amber Dusk like any other accepted theme.

Do not create a theme-specific code path unless the existing preset architecture requires a minimal registration entry.

## 7. UI Effects compatibility

Amber Dusk must work with the accepted UI Effects system.

Requirements:

* UI Effects = Off remains flat;
* Tactile uses the same global Secondary Button / active surface Tabs recipe as other themes;
* no Amber-Dusk-specific tactile styling;
* Strength behaves normally;
* semantic colors/rings remain theme-responsive.

## 8. Preserve architecture boundaries

Do not:

* paste the owner-provided Tailwind stylesheet wholesale into the product;
* create a second CSS theme system;
* introduce duplicate CSS custom properties solely to mirror the source file;
* change Theme v3 schema unless an existing supported preset field genuinely cannot represent the supplied value;
* add new dependencies;
* add network behavior;
* change public component APIs;
* change mutation operations solely for this preset;
* change registry counts solely for this preset.

Prefer adapting the supplied values to the current accepted schema.

## 9. Verification

Verify at minimum:

* Amber Dusk appears in the built-in theme list;
* light-mode semantic colors match the supplied source values after Theme v3 mapping;
* dark-mode semantic colors match the supplied source values after Theme v3 mapping;
* dedicated Sidebar colors work in both modes;
* chart colors render correctly;
* typography/radius/shadow/spacing fields map correctly where supported;
* switching between Amber Dusk and existing themes does not leak values;
* reset/history/save/fork/compare remain correct;
* import/export round trip works;
* UI Effects Off/Tactile works;
* Workbench previews remain responsive;
* accessibility/contrast findings are recorded honestly rather than hidden;
* no regression to Design Command, registry, persistence, or mutation boundaries.

## Acceptance

* New built-in theme is named **Amber Dusk**.
* Amber Dusk is available through the existing built-in theme workflow.
* Supplied light/dark semantic color tokens are preserved through the current Theme v3 representation.
* Supplied Sidebar and chart tokens are preserved.
* Supported typography, radius, spacing, and shadow values are mapped into the existing Theme v3 model without parallel styling infrastructure.
* The owner-provided stylesheet is treated as source data, not copied as a second theme runtime.
* Light/dark switching is correct.
* Theme switching does not leak Amber Dusk values into other presets.
* History/reset/save/fork/compare/import/export remain correct.
* UI Effects works normally with Amber Dusk.
* No Theme v4, new dependency, network behavior, new registry resource, or unrelated architecture change is introduced unless source inspection proves a current Theme v3 limitation that must be reconciled explicitly.
